      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, I believe that this override would not be strictly necessary once Java modules implement `ImageInterface`, which cc and rust modules currently utilize, and [create variants per partition](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/android/image.go;drc\u003d47e918450f83fc5f2680c0a3f7d6d1209e031e7c;l\u003d125) and set the containers there. \n\nPrior to this work, the build system already has scattered information about which partitions each modules belong to, which are mostly set in a limited number of mutators (e.g. `ImageMutator`, `ApexInfoMutator`). I believe that the significance of this work is introducing a mechanism that collects the scattered information and defining how each containers interact.\n\nI am unsure which of the two approaches are more Soong-native and scalable:\n- Computing each containers in the related mutators and storing the information in `ModuleBase` (suggested)\n- Computing all containers in `ModuleBase.GenerateBuildActions` after all mutators are run and storing the information via provider (implemented)\n\n@spandandas@google.com @ccross@android.com Would you have any thoughts on this?",
